WEBVTT

00:00:26.980 --> 00:00:30.470
Futakoi Alternative

00:00:26.980 --> 00:00:30.470
Translation by AnimeYuki

00:00:30.510 --> 00:00:33.780
Run at once towards a dream

00:00:30.510 --> 00:00:33.780
yume no mukou e ikkini hashitte yo

00:00:35.260 --> 00:00:38.750
Let’s meet and laugh away yesterday’s troubles

00:00:35.260 --> 00:00:38.750
nayameru kinou wo fungiri warai aou

00:00:40.090 --> 00:00:44.830
When our memories were here,

00:00:40.090 --> 00:00:44.830
omoide ga itta no toki mo

00:00:44.830 --> 00:00:47.020
even though we are deeply hurt, go straight on

00:00:44.830 --> 00:00:47.020
kizu wo fukai no ni massugu mae ni

00:00:47.020 --> 00:00:49.320
GO TO NEW WORLD

00:00:49.320 --> 00:00:54.440
I can feel it in the wind

00:00:49.320 --> 00:00:54.440
kaze no naka kanjiteru yo

00:00:54.440 --> 00:00:57.950
The hot beat is shining

00:00:54.440 --> 00:00:57.950
atsui kodou kagayaku yo

00:00:57.950 --> 00:01:00.580
especially now…

00:00:57.950 --> 00:01:00.580
ima koso

00:01:02.930 --> 00:01:07.630
surely, always, you’ll be by my side

00:01:02.930 --> 00:01:07.630
kitto zutto soba ni iru yo ne

00:01:07.630 --> 00:01:12.630
Keep on running the way to the future.

00:01:07.630 --> 00:01:12.630
mirai no michi wo hashiri tsuzukeyou

00:01:12.630 --> 00:01:17.270
more and more, no matter what happens

00:01:12.630 --> 00:01:17.270
motto motto nani ga okitemo

00:01:17.270 --> 00:01:21.480
half our tears become double smiles

00:01:17.270 --> 00:01:21.480
namida wa hanbun nibai no egao ni naru

00:01:21.480 --> 00:01:24.030
forever

00:01:21.480 --> 00:01:24.030
itsudemo

00:02:10.230 --> 00:02:11.580
How’s business?

00:02:11.580 --> 00:02:12.680
Same as usual.

00:02:12.680 --> 00:02:14.730
Kitamura Kogote’s second son…

00:02:14.730 --> 00:02:17.930
He was in the same clubs and activities as you in high school.

00:02:17.930 --> 00:02:18.680
Kankurou?

00:02:18.680 --> 00:02:21.780
It seems he’s gotten himself a wife and has settled down.

00:02:21.780 --> 00:02:22.830
Oh, really?

00:02:24.780 --> 00:02:26.280
The same as usual…

00:02:26.280 --> 00:02:27.500
Leave me alone, please!

00:02:29.030 --> 00:02:30.380
I’m going first.

00:02:34.030 --> 00:02:35.480
Sara-chan?

00:02:35.480 --> 00:02:36.230
Hmm?

00:02:38.030 --> 00:02:39.830
“The same as usual,” she said…

00:02:40.730 --> 00:02:41.280
Hmm.

00:02:42.080 --> 00:02:43.880
What is “the same as usual”?

00:02:49.930 --> 00:02:53.890
Although, for honor’s sake, I’d say I’ve really matured at least a little bit.

00:02:55.980 --> 00:02:57.080
Futaba Rentarou.

00:02:57.080 --> 00:02:58.900
Born and raised in Nikotama.

00:02:59.630 --> 00:03:00.980
Gender: Male.

00:03:00.980 --> 00:03:02.280
Age: 21 years old.

00:03:02.280 --> 00:03:04.230
Height: 175 cm.

00:03:04.230 --> 00:03:05.660
Weight: 62 kg.

00:03:06.630 --> 00:03:09.330
Hobby: Fishing for crayfish
on the Tamagawa’s riverbed.

00:03:10.030 --> 00:03:11.580
Job: Private detective.

00:03:12.480 --> 00:03:14.130
Family: None.

00:03:14.780 --> 00:03:16.130
Oh! Nidaime!

00:03:16.130 --> 00:03:16.880
Morning.

00:03:16.880 --> 00:03:18.330
Good morning, Gen-san.

00:03:18.330 --> 00:03:20.230
Fishing for crayfish again
at this time of day?

00:03:20.230 --> 00:03:24.130
Of course! You’re looking lovely as usual, twin ladies.

00:03:24.130 --> 00:03:25.080
Yay!

00:03:25.080 --> 00:03:26.330
To tell the truth…

00:03:26.330 --> 00:03:28.280
Business was never good enough that I needed to hire assistants,

00:03:28.280 --> 00:03:30.930
and as far I can remember,
I’ve always been called Nidaime.

00:03:30.930 --> 00:03:31.430
But…

00:03:31.230 --> 00:03:31.990
Wah!

00:03:35.530 --> 00:03:36.330
Nidaime!

00:03:36.780 --> 00:03:37.620
Good morning, Nidaime.

00:03:38.130 --> 00:03:39.160
Nidaime.

00:03:39.280 --> 00:03:40.080
What? What?

00:03:40.080 --> 00:03:44.180
Where did you take the twins
so early in the morning, Nidaime?

00:03:44.180 --> 00:03:45.530
Morning, twins.

00:03:45.530 --> 00:03:46.670
Good morning!

00:03:46.830 --> 00:03:50.580
Recently, the guy staying at my place has been coming back late,

00:03:50.580 --> 00:03:53.730
I wonder if I can get you to
investigate for me just this once?

00:03:53.730 --> 00:03:55.180
It’s expensive.

00:03:55.180 --> 00:03:56.180
Eh…

00:03:56.180 --> 00:03:58.380
But don’t I always take care of you?

00:03:58.550 --> 00:04:01.880
You haven’t seen your calico cat
since yesterday evening?

00:04:01.880 --> 00:04:05.580
How much will it cost for you to search for it, Nidaime?

00:04:05.580 --> 00:04:07.630
Oh, I don’t need that sort of money.

00:04:07.630 --> 00:04:10.020
We’re carrying out a free campaign!

00:04:10.150 --> 00:04:12.180
Nidaime! Morning!

00:04:12.180 --> 00:04:13.680
Hey! Watch out for the cars!

00:04:13.680 --> 00:04:14.930
I KNOW!

00:04:14.930 --> 00:04:16.480
Nidaime, heads up!

00:04:17.180 --> 00:04:18.780
Oh! Bad throw!

00:04:20.080 --> 00:04:22.240
Well, to put it extravagantly, there’s no end to it.

00:04:22.730 --> 00:04:27.780
The way people call me “Nidaime” is proof of the challenges I’ve endured.

00:04:41.830 --> 00:04:44.030
But, before that…

00:04:44.030 --> 00:04:46.530
There are so many things I need to say.

00:04:48.380 --> 00:04:50.480
First is my wonderful detective business.

00:04:50.480 --> 00:04:52.340
It’s about my detective life.

00:04:52.340 --> 00:04:53.780
YAY!

00:04:53.780 --> 00:04:54.280
Huh?

00:04:54.280 --> 00:04:55.830
What’s “deteel hip”?

00:04:55.830 --> 00:04:57.380
Detective!

00:04:57.380 --> 00:05:00.570
Also, in order to understand that…
a few images.

00:05:01.330 --> 00:05:02.530
Image number one.

00:05:03.280 --> 00:05:07.030
The image of a set of curious twins
standing at the entrance of the agency.

00:05:13.630 --> 00:05:15.130
Image number two.

00:05:15.580 --> 00:05:17.430
The image of my shock

00:05:17.430 --> 00:05:20.130
at seeing a UFO through the hole in the agency’s ceiling.

00:05:27.530 --> 00:05:29.380
Thank you for your call.

00:05:29.380 --> 00:05:31.530
This is the Futaba Detective Agency.

00:05:31.530 --> 00:05:33.180
Image number three.

00:05:33.180 --> 00:05:37.150
The day known as “today” begins with a call from an unknown client.

00:05:38.780 --> 00:05:39.480
UFO?

00:05:50.430 --> 00:05:51.290
That’s why!

00:05:51.290 --> 00:05:54.130
Haven’t I said answering
the phone is my job?!

00:05:54.130 --> 00:05:55.580
I heard it properly!

00:05:55.580 --> 00:05:58.980
“I’II go there in an hour.
I’ll tell you the details then.”

00:05:58.980 --> 00:06:01.730
Well then, Shirogane Soujyu-san, what’s the client’s name?

00:06:01.730 --> 00:06:03.880
I asked. He didn’t say, though.

00:06:03.880 --> 00:06:06.080
Your duties are cleaning and cooking.

00:06:06.080 --> 00:06:07.430
As for helping out with the detective agency work…

00:06:07.430 --> 00:06:10.480
I want to help out too! I want to! I want to!

00:06:10.480 --> 00:06:13.330
Don’t you have your girly work?!

00:06:13.330 --> 00:06:13.940
That’s why…!

00:06:13.940 --> 00:06:16.610
I want to! I want to! I want to! I wa…

00:06:16.610 --> 00:06:21.430
But if you did everything,
I wouldn’t have anything to do!!

00:06:24.280 --> 00:06:26.930
Boss!

00:06:26.930 --> 00:06:29.620
Which one of us should answer the phone?!

00:06:30.880 --> 00:06:33.480
It’s best to make idle conversation
when the situation gets awkward like this.

00:06:33.480 --> 00:06:36.330
Anyway, let’s limit the harmless and inoffensive stories to this.

00:06:36.730 --> 00:06:39.300
Twins, a slightly strange story.

00:06:40.430 --> 00:06:42.380
1957.

00:06:42.380 --> 00:06:44.180
In Ohio, in America,

00:06:44.180 --> 00:06:46.730
twins named Jim and James were born.

00:06:47.630 --> 00:06:50.580
Four weeks after birth,
they were given up for adoption.

00:06:50.580 --> 00:06:54.630
They did not know of each other’s existence for forty years.

00:06:54.630 --> 00:06:57.730
One day, these twins unexpectedly bumped into each other.

00:06:57.730 --> 00:07:00.030
There were some coincidental similarities.

00:07:00.830 --> 00:07:02.530
They drove the same cars,

00:07:03.140 --> 00:07:05.530
they married women with the same names,

00:07:05.980 --> 00:07:08.330
their eldest sons had the same birthday,

00:07:08.330 --> 00:07:12.280
and, Jim worked as a gynecologist.

00:07:12.280 --> 00:07:14.280
James… didn’t.

00:07:19.380 --> 00:07:20.130
Good day!

00:07:20.930 --> 00:07:24.230
Hello, madam. Today we have fresh produce.

00:07:25.970 --> 00:07:28.080
One hour has passed.

00:07:28.080 --> 00:07:29.280
The client probably won’t come.

00:07:30.480 --> 00:07:33.430
But, that’s what he said on the phone.

00:07:33.430 --> 00:07:35.280
He said that he’d come in an hour.

00:07:35.930 --> 00:07:36.580
Yeah.

00:07:37.130 --> 00:07:38.630
Something must have happened.

00:07:38.630 --> 00:07:40.180
Like the trains might have stopped,

00:07:40.180 --> 00:07:42.330
or maybe he suddenly got sick,

00:07:42.330 --> 00:07:43.080
something like that.

00:07:45.230 --> 00:07:46.430
Sara-chan.

00:07:46.430 --> 00:07:50.330
About earlier… I’m sorry about
answering the phone on my own.

00:07:50.330 --> 00:07:52.080
Nah, it’s okay.

00:07:52.080 --> 00:07:55.680
More importantly, there’s a
mountain of other stuff we gotta do!

00:07:55.680 --> 00:07:56.580
That’s right!

00:07:56.580 --> 00:07:58.000
We don’t know how long we’ll have to deal with this tedious stuff,

00:07:58.000 --> 00:07:59.130
so let’s quit wasting time and finish it up!

00:07:59.130 --> 00:08:00.030
Seconded!

00:08:00.030 --> 00:08:00.630
By the way…

00:08:00.630 --> 00:08:01.830
All right, I’m done!

00:08:01.830 --> 00:08:02.730
Look, you guys.

00:08:03.530 --> 00:08:08.330
Well, for the time being, I’ll try to talk in an inoffensive manner…

00:08:10.830 --> 00:08:11.480
Yeah, that surely…

00:08:11.480 --> 00:08:14.640
Dear Jim-sama, James-sama…

00:08:14.980 --> 00:08:17.640
For the time being, may I ask you your names?

00:08:18.030 --> 00:08:19.330
Shirogane Soujyu.

00:08:20.180 --> 00:08:21.650
Shirogane Sara.

00:08:22.230 --> 00:08:24.380
So, what is this business of yours?

00:08:24.380 --> 00:08:25.030
How tasteless.

00:08:25.030 --> 00:08:25.650
Huh?

00:08:26.180 --> 00:08:27.070
Sara-chan.

00:08:27.730 --> 00:08:29.650
Who decorated this place?

00:08:29.650 --> 00:08:32.480
It… It was me… What about it?

00:08:32.480 --> 00:08:33.330
It’s very tasteless.

00:08:33.330 --> 00:08:34.230
It’s so old-manish.

00:08:34.880 --> 00:08:36.330
Especially that reed mat.

00:08:36.330 --> 00:08:40.130
You can only find those in public baths or in the rooms of delinquent girls these days.

00:08:40.130 --> 00:08:41.830
Don’t say stupid things.

00:08:41.830 --> 00:08:43.380
Nowadays, people seem
to do stuff like that.

00:08:44.380 --> 00:08:47.680
Indeed, now that you mention it, I feel the same way about it.

00:08:47.680 --> 00:08:48.930
Anyway, it’s useless.

00:08:48.930 --> 00:08:51.140
Or shall we say, it seems likely that he doesn’t have a girlfriend…

00:08:51.140 --> 00:08:53.230
Then again, he really
doesn’t seem to have one.

00:08:53.230 --> 00:08:55.380
He’s horrible. I’m disillusioned.

00:08:55.630 --> 00:08:57.780
This sort of place is so…

00:08:59.380 --> 00:09:02.280
Men should be like “this is cute,” or something…

00:09:02.280 --> 00:09:06.780
They are only alike in looks.
Other than that, they are exact opposites.

00:09:06.780 --> 00:09:09.980
I guess older people can only afford to indulge in old men’s hobbies.

00:09:12.480 --> 00:09:14.480
Even so, in these two years,

00:09:14.480 --> 00:09:19.620
though our relationship is  pretty carefree, I’m beginning to understand it more.

00:09:33.280 --> 00:09:34.390
Here I go.

00:09:35.630 --> 00:09:38.180
Oh yeah…

00:09:38.180 --> 00:09:51.780
GO GO GO GO…

00:09:41.630 --> 00:09:42.600
What, what?!

00:09:43.280 --> 00:09:44.380
Sara-chan,

00:09:44.380 --> 00:09:47.480
do you think this will work for the flower’s soil?

00:09:47.480 --> 00:09:48.480
SARA-CHAN!

00:09:48.480 --> 00:09:51.180
DO YOU THINK THIS WILL WORK FOR THE FLOWER’S SOIL?

00:09:51.780 --> 00:09:52.730
Okay!

00:09:52.730 --> 00:09:54.580
By the way, should the wall be like this?

00:09:54.580 --> 00:09:56.110
It’s right on the mark!

00:09:56.110 --> 00:09:57.930
BOSS!

00:09:57.930 --> 00:09:59.630
Right! Right! OKAY!

00:09:59.630 --> 00:10:00.750
It’s right on the mark!

00:10:02.120 --> 00:10:03.530
BOSS!

00:10:03.530 --> 00:10:04.330
Okay! OKAY!!

00:10:04.330 --> 00:10:06.000
I’m pouring the coffee now!

00:10:06.390 --> 00:10:08.280
Little things started to pile up,

00:10:08.280 --> 00:10:11.010
and our relationship began to grow a little.

00:10:11.010 --> 00:10:13.680
One, two, three, four…

00:10:15.080 --> 00:10:15.730
Huh?

00:10:25.690 --> 00:10:28.430
How much sugar do you want?

00:10:30.230 --> 00:10:31.900
…then much, much more…

00:11:12.080 --> 00:11:14.580
The client isn’t coming, is he?

00:11:14.580 --> 00:11:18.530
This is most likely because he had
some sort of really urgent business.

00:11:18.530 --> 00:11:19.930
Such as?

00:11:19.930 --> 00:11:20.980
Hmm…

00:11:20.980 --> 00:11:24.680
Urgent business which
far surpasses our imagination.

00:11:24.680 --> 00:11:25.780
I see…

00:11:25.780 --> 00:11:26.830
Say.

00:11:26.830 --> 00:11:27.630
Hmm?

00:11:27.630 --> 00:11:28.780
It’s Sunday.

00:11:28.780 --> 00:11:30.330
Don’t you have stuff to do?

00:11:30.330 --> 00:11:33.230
Rather than wasting time in this broken-down agency,

00:11:33.230 --> 00:11:34.680
why don’t you do stuff like
going to the movies,

00:11:34.680 --> 00:11:36.480
helping out around the house,

00:11:36.480 --> 00:11:38.280
bumming around till late afternoon,

00:11:46.880 --> 00:11:48.310
…or going on a date?

00:11:57.580 --> 00:11:59.280
Well, it’s fine though.

00:12:09.530 --> 00:12:10.930
The sky is blue.

00:12:11.880 --> 00:12:12.930
The clouds are white.

00:12:14.830 --> 00:12:18.230
The appointment… changed to 3 pm.

00:12:26.260 --> 00:12:27.630
Oh!

00:12:27.630 --> 00:12:28.480
Caught it. Caught it.

00:12:49.530 --> 00:12:50.500
Three o’clock.

00:12:51.030 --> 00:12:56.050
So in other words, as of today, we’ve decided to exchange roles for cooking!

00:12:56.050 --> 00:12:57.710
That’s GREAT!

00:12:57.710 --> 00:12:59.680
First up is Sara-chan!

00:12:59.680 --> 00:13:00.760
Yay!

00:13:01.380 --> 00:13:03.720
Well then, everyone, please eat up.

00:13:03.720 --> 00:13:05.480
Let’s eat.

00:13:05.480 --> 00:13:06.970
We’re done eating.

00:13:09.190 --> 00:13:10.580
Phew, I’m done, I’m done. Man, I’m stuffed.

00:13:10.580 --> 00:13:12.180
I feel like eating pudding.

00:13:12.180 --> 00:13:15.080
Yeah. Yeah. Well, Sara-chan’s cooking is pretty good.

00:13:15.080 --> 00:13:17.680
From now on, Sara-chan
can do all the cooking.

00:13:17.680 --> 00:13:18.930
Yes, yes.

00:13:18.930 --> 00:13:21.330
Anyway, the client should be coming anytime now.

00:13:21.330 --> 00:13:23.530
Isn’t it our job to tidy up?

00:13:23.530 --> 00:13:24.550
Yes. Yes.

00:13:30.680 --> 00:13:32.580
Eh?! What? There’s still a lot remaining.

00:13:32.580 --> 00:13:33.530
I’m gonna eat it, I’m gonna eat it!

00:13:33.530 --> 00:13:33.980
Yum, yum.

00:13:33.980 --> 00:13:35.830
Well it’s not like it’s bad but…

00:13:35.830 --> 00:13:36.460
Yeah. Yeah.

00:13:36.460 --> 00:13:38.980
Hot! HOT! IT’S LITERALLY BURNING!

00:13:38.980 --> 00:13:39.460
Yeah. Yeah.

00:13:53.330 --> 00:13:55.580
Rentarou!

00:13:54.730 --> 00:13:55.580
There, there.

00:13:55.580 --> 00:13:56.930
It you want to cry, then cry.

00:13:56.930 --> 00:13:58.880
Cry until your sadness ends.

00:13:58.880 --> 00:13:59.980
And then, eat this.

00:14:00.980 --> 00:14:03.080
GYAAAAAAAAAAAK!!

00:14:03.080 --> 00:14:03.830
Sigh.

00:14:04.230 --> 00:14:05.080
Sigh.

00:14:10.380 --> 00:14:11.780
Another fire?

00:14:12.330 --> 00:14:15.080
Yeah… Seems like it.

00:14:15.080 --> 00:14:16.580
Just last week too…

00:14:16.580 --> 00:14:17.430
Yeah…

00:14:17.430 --> 00:14:20.110
It was also burning wildly last week…

00:14:21.080 --> 00:14:25.300
Though I’m saying this for the sake of honor, I really didn’t cause those fires.

00:14:25.970 --> 00:14:29.260
It’s inaccurate to use a gentle word like “fire” to describe the previous events, though.

00:14:30.930 --> 00:14:35.330
An explosion blew my house
to pieces, blew off the roof, and…

00:14:37.330 --> 00:14:37.930
and…

00:14:39.080 --> 00:14:41.330
still, there were things that didn’t get destroyed.

00:15:33.280 --> 00:15:34.980
I had a nostalgic dream.

00:15:44.280 --> 00:15:45.580
E-Everyone!

00:15:45.580 --> 00:15:47.830
This is not a scene from a movie!

00:15:47.830 --> 00:15:50.530
This is reality,
Tokyo’s city of Futagotamagawa!

00:15:50.530 --> 00:15:52.630
The fire is still spreading right now!

00:15:55.130 --> 00:15:57.060
You damned idiot!

00:15:57.630 --> 00:16:01.080
How dare you climb up on people’s chimneys without permission!

00:16:00.380 --> 00:16:01.080
Grandma!

00:16:01.080 --> 00:16:03.880
Quick! Let’s go or we won’t be able to evacuate in time!

00:16:03.880 --> 00:16:04.780
Crap!!

00:16:04.780 --> 00:16:06.130
You alien bastard!

00:16:06.130 --> 00:16:10.080
We’re gonna get up there and blow you to smithereens!

00:16:08.280 --> 00:16:10.080
Indeed…

00:16:10.080 --> 00:16:12.530
Though I’m a squid, I don’t know whether or not to abduct more people,

00:16:12.530 --> 00:16:16.930
so I’ll just burn this world until there is nobody left but squids!

00:16:16.930 --> 00:16:18.430
Believe what you will, deny what you will,

00:16:18.430 --> 00:16:22.180
no matter what, I’ll make use of it.
I am just going to KILL YOU!

00:16:22.180 --> 00:16:24.080
RAGING FIRE!

00:16:33.530 --> 00:16:35.580
The criminal is an unidentified squid.

00:16:35.580 --> 00:16:36.480
A squid?

00:16:36.480 --> 00:16:38.270
Yes, it certainly is a squid.

00:16:38.270 --> 00:16:40.830
We don’t really know anything other than that it’s a squid.

00:16:40.830 --> 00:16:43.580
The counterstrike forces aren’t here yet.

00:16:43.580 --> 00:16:46.320
The desperate actions of the police were futile, and the city is…

00:17:01.530 --> 00:17:02.980
What idiots.

00:17:02.980 --> 00:17:04.620
It… It’s impossible, I said!

00:17:05.230 --> 00:17:10.130
N-N-N-No matter how you think about it, we’ll die!

00:17:10.340 --> 00:17:12.930
By the way, this is me 5 years ago.

00:17:12.930 --> 00:17:16.050
Contrary to my sharp appearance, I was seriously inexperienced.

00:17:17.580 --> 00:17:18.680
Are you going to run away?

00:17:18.680 --> 00:17:20.080
It’s not about running away!

00:17:20.080 --> 00:17:23.730
Why do we have to go and fight that squid thing?

00:17:25.980 --> 00:17:28.650
Answer me! Just try and answer me!

00:17:40.380 --> 00:17:41.670
Because I love it.

00:17:41.980 --> 00:17:42.380
Huh?

00:17:43.230 --> 00:17:45.080
Because I love this Nikotama!

00:17:52.300 --> 00:17:54.130
Life is long…

00:17:54.130 --> 00:17:56.230
whether you bum around in front of a convenience store,

00:17:56.230 --> 00:17:59.520
or run away with a stolen bike, or do whatever you feel like.

00:17:59.520 --> 00:18:02.230
But, at least, you must know this:

00:18:02.230 --> 00:18:05.980
For a man, there comes a time when he has to protect what must be protected.

00:18:05.980 --> 00:18:07.930
At that time, what action will you take?

00:18:07.930 --> 00:18:11.530
In a man’s lifetime, there is one moment when everything will be decided.

00:18:13.430 --> 00:18:15.430
D-Dad.

00:18:17.580 --> 00:18:18.430
Son.

00:18:19.880 --> 00:18:21.210
It it were you, what would you do?

00:18:23.680 --> 00:18:24.690
If it was me…

00:18:26.080 --> 00:18:27.170
If you were a father…

00:18:29.180 --> 00:18:30.720
you’d do it like this!

00:18:33.080 --> 00:18:35.530
Damn it! Are we at our wits’ end?

00:18:37.430 --> 00:18:38.140
That is…

00:18:49.430 --> 00:18:50.530
Are you scared?

00:18:50.530 --> 00:18:52.880
I’m fine, you damn bastard!!

00:18:52.880 --> 00:18:54.330
I see!

00:18:54.330 --> 00:18:56.380
This is the first time you’ve charmed me, my son.

00:18:56.380 --> 00:18:58.200
In that case, I shall impart it to you now!

00:18:58.200 --> 00:19:00.730
The Futaba Family
One Hit Striking Technique!

00:19:03.280 --> 00:19:04.920
Squid?

00:19:04.920 --> 00:19:06.780
SQUID!

00:19:07.830 --> 00:19:09.830
Son, I’m leaving the steering up to you!

00:19:13.760 --> 00:19:16.630
Watch me.  I’ll show you want real a man does!

00:19:17.260 --> 00:19:19.630
There will be no victory for you!

00:19:19.630 --> 00:19:21.550
In that case…

00:19:23.230 --> 00:19:26.430
In that case I’m gonna
show you my special attack!

00:19:32.780 --> 00:19:33.630
Ouch!

00:19:42.230 --> 00:19:43.830
That’s me 5 years ago.

00:19:44.830 --> 00:19:47.330
My ineptitude hasn’t really
changed since then,

00:19:47.330 --> 00:19:49.530
but I resolutely decided to lead the life of a man,

00:19:49.530 --> 00:19:51.030
in those moments when my heart wavered.

00:19:57.130 --> 00:19:58.380
I’m home!

00:19:58.380 --> 00:20:00.080
Ah, they finally came back!

00:20:00.080 --> 00:20:01.430
YOU!

00:20:02.350 --> 00:20:04.880
In the end, the client didn’t come.

00:20:04.880 --> 00:20:05.980
It’s my fault.

00:20:06.480 --> 00:20:07.980
I didn’t say that. I didn’t say that.

00:20:07.980 --> 00:20:09.030
Oh well.

00:20:09.680 --> 00:20:12.780
The income of the Futaba Detective Agency today sums up to zero.

00:20:12.780 --> 00:20:15.880
And Sunday is… over.

00:20:15.880 --> 00:20:17.260
I wonder what happened.

00:20:34.970 --> 00:20:36.780
Oh!

00:20:36.780 --> 00:20:38.100
UFO!!!

00:20:40.520 --> 00:20:41.420
Outside, outside! Quickly…!

00:20:43.730 --> 00:20:44.780
Hurry up, hurry up!

00:20:44.780 --> 00:20:47.100
Outside, outside! Quickly! Quickly!

00:20:48.280 --> 00:20:49.380
Oh, Nidaime!

00:20:49.380 --> 00:20:50.680
Where are you going this late?

00:20:50.680 --> 00:20:53.150
It’s a UFO, a UFO!

00:20:55.030 --> 00:20:59.780
To tell the truth, business was never good enough that I needed to hire assistants.

00:20:59.780 --> 00:21:01.930
And I’m always being called “Nidaime” by others.

00:21:07.200 --> 00:21:10.310
In the end, I wasn’t able to catch that fish.

00:21:11.330 --> 00:21:14.480
Oh? What’s the matter, Nidaime? You’re in quite a hurry.

00:21:14.480 --> 00:21:15.730
A UFO, a UFO!

00:21:15.730 --> 00:21:17.180
UFO! UFO!

00:21:15.730 --> 00:21:16.520
Huh?

00:21:18.180 --> 00:21:22.230
Of course, there’s no way a UFO would appear on such an ordinary day.

00:21:23.880 --> 00:21:24.380
But…

00:21:30.780 --> 00:21:33.880
Well, if I were to keep going, I could ramble on forever…

00:21:33.880 --> 00:21:35.680
It’s just that I’m sure I’d end up paying for it.

00:21:36.280 --> 00:21:40.030
So, that’s our wonderful detective business, our “detective life”.

00:21:40.630 --> 00:21:43.880
So then, what sort of story
would you like to hear tomorrow?

00:21:45.730 --> 00:21:48.330
All’s right with the world.

00:21:48.330 --> 00:21:51.000
As expected, as expected.

00:21:53.180 --> 00:21:55.980
Hi, this is the Futaba Detective Agency.

00:21:55.980 --> 00:21:57.730
We are not here at the moment.

00:21:57.730 --> 00:22:01.330
Please leave us a message with your request after the beep. Thanks!

00:22:02.530 --> 00:22:04.580
A-Ah, excuse me!

00:22:04.580 --> 00:22:09.380
Even though I had called you earlier, some circumstances messed up my plans for today.

00:22:09.380 --> 00:22:12.830
I was thinking of rescheduling that appointment…

00:22:14.240 --> 00:22:19.920
We are here.

00:22:14.240 --> 00:22:19.750
bokura wa koko ni iru

00:22:20.250 --> 00:22:27.320
We will be here.

00:22:20.250 --> 00:22:27.320
bokura ga koko ni aru

00:22:27.660 --> 00:22:32.640
The slow time is

00:22:27.660 --> 00:22:32.640
yuruyaka na jikan ga

00:22:32.870 --> 00:22:39.570
flowing in this room.

00:22:32.870 --> 00:22:39.570
nagareteru kono heya de

00:22:40.210 --> 00:22:43.170
Even if the summer days vanish,

00:22:40.210 --> 00:22:43.170
natsu no hi ga kiete mo

00:22:43.400 --> 00:22:47.230
the smiles that remain

00:22:43.400 --> 00:22:47.230
nokoru egao tachi

00:22:47.350 --> 00:22:54.110
are a chain of happiness up to this point.

00:22:47.350 --> 00:22:54.110
kocchi made shiawase no rensa

00:22:54.350 --> 00:22:59.950
Ah, the meaning of honesty,

00:22:54.350 --> 00:22:59.950
aa sunaosa no imi

00:23:00.230 --> 00:23:08.290
is within the innermost depths of your heart.

00:23:00.230 --> 00:23:08.290
KOKORO no zutto zutto oku no hou e

00:23:08.490 --> 00:23:13.670
Hey, the days are wonderful

00:23:08.490 --> 00:23:13.670
nee subarashii hibi

00:23:13.910 --> 00:23:21.430
in the midst of weakness and anxiety.

00:23:13.910 --> 00:23:21.430
yowasa to fuan no naka de shitte

00:23:21.460 --> 00:23:27.980
I won’t say goodbye, Because forever

00:23:21.460 --> 00:23:27.980
sayonara wa iwanai yo datte itsumademo

00:23:28.130 --> 00:23:33.260
the days will be unchanged.

00:23:28.130 --> 00:23:33.260
kawaru koto no nai hibi

00:23:33.390 --> 00:23:40.100
Surely forever. M

00:23:33.390 --> 00:23:40.100
kitto itsumademo

